<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sindi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sindians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sindi were an ancient people of the Taman peninsula and the lower Kuban in the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, often counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeotians">Maeotians</a>. Greek cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorgippia">Gorgippia</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anapa">Anapa</a>, grew in their land, and their kingdom came under the Bosporan kings in the 4th century BCE, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartocid-dynasty">Spartocids</a> styled themselves kings of the Sindi.</p></div>
